diff --git a/tests/README.long-calls.md b/tests/README.long-calls.md
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/README.long-calls.md
@@ -0,0 +1,56 @@
+# Per-declaration Thumb long calls
+
+The Thumb C and C++ backends already support `-mlong-calls` for an entire
+translation unit. This correction also accepts `__attribute__((long_call))`
+on a function declaration. Only references to that declaration use the
+existing indirect interworking path; unmarked functions keep their direct
+calls and original instruction selection. No symbol name or address is tested.
+
+The marker is retained on the function's RTL symbol, including redeclarations,
+and consulted by both void and value-returning call expansion. This is a
+declaration attribute, not a new function-pointer type attribute. The ARM
+callee's actual ELF symbol supplies its address and mode; no alias, fixed
+register, instruction rewrite, or file-wide flag is needed.
+
+`long-call.c` is compiled once as C and once as C++. `long-call-start.s`
+provides near Thumb callees and far ARM callees. `long-call.lds` deliberately
+separates the latter by more than a Thumb BL's range. The executable checks
+scalar, void and two-word structure returns together with unaffected near
+calls. After a normal `./build.sh`, run with `arm-none-eabi` binutils and
+`qemu-arm`:
+
+```sh
+tmpdir=$(mktemp -d)
+arm-none-eabi-as -mcpu=arm7tdmi tests/long-call-start.s -o "$tmpdir/start.o"
+arm-none-eabi-cpp -x c -P tests/long-call.c -o "$tmpdir/c.i"
+./agbcc -O2 -mthumb-interwork -Werror -o "$tmpdir/c.s" < "$tmpdir/c.i"
+arm-none-eabi-cpp -x c++ -P tests/long-call.c -o "$tmpdir/cpp.i"
+./agbcp -quiet -fno-exceptions -fno-rtti -fvtable-thunks \
+    -O2 -mthumb-interwork -Werror -o "$tmpdir/cpp.s" < "$tmpdir/cpp.i"
+for mode in c cpp; do
+    arm-none-eabi-as -mcpu=arm7tdmi "$tmpdir/$mode.s" -o "$tmpdir/$mode.o"
+    arm-none-eabi-objdump -dr "$tmpdir/$mode.o"
+    arm-none-eabi-ld -T tests/long-call.lds "$tmpdir/start.o" \
+        "$tmpdir/$mode.o" -o "$tmpdir/$mode.elf"
+    qemu-arm "$tmpdir/$mode.elf" || exit "$?"
+done
+```
+
+Both executions must return zero. Each `far_*` target must have an ABS32
+relocation, not a THM_CALL relocation; `near_value` and `near_sink` must still
+have THM_CALL relocations. The original toolchain rejects this attribute under
+`-Werror`; removing it cannot link these out-of-range direct calls.
+
+## 中文说明
+
+两套 Thumb 前端原有全文件 `-mlong-calls`，现补充函数声明上的
+`long_call` 属性，只改变被标记声明的调用，未标记的近调用保持
+原有指令选择。属性随函数 RTL 符号保留，并在 void 与有返回值的
+调用展开时使用；支持函数声明，不声称新增函数指针类型属性。
+没有判断符号名或地址，也不使用别名、固定寄存器、指令修补或
+全文件优化选项。ARM 入口的真实 ELF 符号提供地址和执行模式。
+
+上述同一测试分别以 C、C++ 编译，实际调用近处 Thumb 函数和远处
+ARM 函数，检查标量、void、两字结构体返回及普通近调用。链接位置
+仅属于独立测试，用于保证远处确实超出 Thumb BL 范围，不是任何
+游戏地址。两次执行都应返回零，重定位类型须符合上面的检查。
